{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For from a vine, etc.</b> Meaning, He gives a reason for their being recognized, and for what precedes it: ״אָמַרְתִּי אַפְאֵיהֶם.״ And His saying ״מִגֶּפֶן״ — I have already made known that whatever exists in holiness has its counterpart in the sitra achra (the other side), as it says (Ecclesiastes 7:14): ״גַּם אֶת זֶה לְעֻמַּת זֶה עָשָׂה״, etc. And Israel are likened to a vine (Genesis Rabbah 99:8), as it is written (Psalms 80:9): ״גֶּפֶן מִמִּצְרַיִם תַּסִּיעַ״, and corresponding to them, when they did evil, He said ״מִגֶּפֶן סְדֹם״ — and the vine is the evil tree of the grasp of the wicked, as Scripture concludes: ״עֲנָבֵמוֹ עִנְּבֵי רוֹשׁ״, etc. And since they merely grasp hold of it and not all their branches come from it, therefore He said ״מִגֶּפֶן״ and did not say ״כִּי גֶפֶן סְדֹם גַּפְנָם״, and He chose of all things the evil Sodom, because their measure was filled like Sodom's." "<b>And His saying</b> ״וּמִשַּׁדְמוֹת עֲמוֹרָה״ — for just as in the branches of the holy tree there is one fence above another fence, and the higher one is assigned to it a masculine name by virtue of its being an effluent, and the lower one is assigned to it a feminine name by virtue of its receiving effluence, so too did He liken the grasps in the evil root to two fences: the first fence is called גֶּפֶן (vine), and the second fence is called שָׂדֶה (field). And the discerning one will understand by their analogy in holiness, and his eyes will be illumined:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:38.034020342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}